      "spam": false,
      "value": "I mean, best you can do is... simply not play with people who do not wish to play fair.  Better to play with friends.\n\nI do agree it's BS,  though I personnaly would prefer a system like... the bigger one is, the more HP they have, and vice versa.  someone tiny would be killed in a single hit... or killed by being stepped on AND they do less damage.\n\nhowever... I do not think any of this is possible to really do, just an ideal that would be neat if it could.\n\nHaving height limits in the game would be nice.\n\nThe main thing suggested here... would actually be a means to actually detect size of avatars, to allow creator of games and worlds to be able to customize how rules apply to avatars.  More tools to create games based on Avatars, and if they implement Tags for a model, those could also be used for coding.\n\nJust my thoughts on your suggestion.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-31T11:31:52.607Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Many players tend to abuse avatars in CTF and other games by choosing very tiny avatars that can barely be hit, like the small knuckles avatar or tiny anime avatars. I think it'll be worth adding some kind of a minimum size requirement to ensure this is not done anymore. We can perhaps use the official robot avatar as a measurement and have some extra room for bigger/smaller avatars than that, within reason.",
